commit e279d5a2991ae1467a7af717115f8a8656d5f101
Author: Daniel28972897 <danyboy28sep@gmail.com>

dt-bindings: misc: convert axis-fifo binding to YAML

This commit converts the text-based axis-fifo binding to a YAML schema to
enable validation via dtbs_check. It preserves all original properties,
including those generated by the Xilinx IP integrator that are currently
ignored by the Linux driver.

> diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/misc/xlnx,axi-fifo-mm-s.ya=
ml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/misc/xlnx,axi-fifo-mm-s.yaml
> new file mode 100644
> index 0000000000000..fffd69b128111
> --- /dev/null
> +++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/misc/xlnx,axi-fifo-mm-s.yaml
[ ... ]
> +  # The following properties are generated by the Xilinx IP integrator
> +  # for this core and may be present in real-world devicetrees, but are
> +  # not currently read by the Linux driver.
> +  xlnx,axi-str-rxd-protocol: true
> +  xlnx,axi-str-txc-protocol: true
> +  xlnx,axi-str-txc-tdata-width: true
> +  xlnx,axi-str-txd-protocol: true
> +  xlnx,axis-tdest-width: true
> +  xlnx,axis-tid-width: true

[Severity: Low]
Does this properties block in
Documentation/devicetree/bindings/misc/xlnx,axi-fifo-mm-s.yaml pass make
dt_binding_check?

The dtschema meta-schema requires all custom vendor-specific properties to
have an explicitly defined type constraint (e.g.,
$ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32).

Setting these vendor properties to true without mandatory $ref type
definitions or descriptions causes a build-time validation failure when
running make dt_binding_check on the added schema.

Will these properties be updated to include the appropriate type constraint=
s?

